TIKI
// HZM coop [user 2026-08-31] BEACH SMOKE SCREEN - white concealing smoke for the m3l1a smoke drop.
//
// Why a new emitter instead of a retail one: EVERY retail smoke emitter is dark burning smoke, not
// screening smoke. ddaysmoke is color 0.2 0.23 0.26, ddaysmoke2 is 0.23 0.23 0.22, tehao_thickSmoke
// and linger_smoke are .2 .2 .2 - all soot. The user asked for white smoke that actually conceals the
// beach, and the only white smoke in the game is the M18 grenade's, which is not reusable here: its
// TIKI is `classname SmokeGrenade` with `toss` and a 30s fuse, i.e. a thrown projectile, not a static
// emitter you can place.
//
// [user 2026-08-31] SPRITE CORRECTED. The first version used smokegrenade_allied.spr, the M18's own
// sprite, on the assumption that color 1 1 1 would make it white. It does not: emitter 'color' is a
// MULTIPLIER over the sprite texture, and the allied smoke grenade is RED signal smoke, so red x white
// is still red - which is what the user saw. vsssource.spr is the sprite every D-Day smoke emitter uses
// (ddaysmoke, ddaysmoke2, linger_smoke) and they all TINT IT DOWN - ddaysmoke to 0.2 0.23 0.26 - which
// is only possible if the base texture is light. At color 1 1 1 it is the white screening smoke wanted.
//
// The particle values are still lifted from models/fx/M18_Smoke_GrenadeExplosion_base.txt (the real
// screening smoke) and re-tuned for a standing area screen rather than a hand grenade:
//   - scalemin/max 1.8/2.8 against M18's 0.2/0.4. The sprite is 128px, so a puff is ~230-360 units
//     across instead of ~26-51. Big puffs are what actually block line of sight.
//   - life 26 and fadedelay 18 against M18's 10 / 7, so the screen stands rather than puffing away.
//   - spawnrate 4 keeps the live particle count near 100 per emitter. Deliberately NOT higher: this is
//     placed 13 times at once on a beach that already runs 50+ actors, and overlapping alpha is the
//     expensive part. Density comes from the puff SIZE, not the count.
//   - no `collision`. The M18 bounces its particles off the world; across a 13-point screen that is a
//     lot of per-particle traces for an effect the player reads as one cloud.
setup
{
	scale 1.0
	path models/fx/dummy
	skelmodel dummy3.skd
}

init
{
	server
	{
		classname effectentity
		notsolid
		rendereffects +dontdraw
	}
	client
	{
		cache vsssource.spr

		originemitter coopscreen
		(
			model vsssource.spr
			color 1 1 1
			spritegridlighting
			alpha 1
			spawnrate 4
			life 26
			scalerate 0.55
			velocity 18
			randvel crandom 26 crandom 26 random 8
			accel 0 0 4
			offset crandom 110 crandom 110 range 0 28
			angles 0 0 random 360
			avelocity 0 0 crandom 12
			scalemin 1.8
			scalemax 2.8
			fadein 1
			fadedelay 18
		)
	}
}

animations
{
	idle dummy3.skc
	start dummy3.skc
	{
		client
		{
			enter emitteron coopscreen
		}
	}
	stop dummy3.skc
	{
		client
		{
			enter emitteroff coopscreen
		}
	}
}
